","Let $X$ be the number of heads in 12 coins. Since the probability of getting a head in a probability is $1/2$, $X$ is a binomial with $n=12$ and $p=1/2$. We want to find the probability $P(X \geq 9)$.
We have
$$P(X=k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} = \binom{12}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^k \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12-k} = \binom{12}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}$$
We want to find $P(X \geq 9) = P(X=9) + P(X=10) + P(X=11) + P(X=12)$.
$$P(X=9) = \binom{12}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \frac{12!}{9!3} \left(\frac{1}{2^{12}}\right) = \frac{12 \times 11 \times 10}{3 \times 2 \times 1} \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = 220 \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = \frac{220}{4096}$$
$$P(X=10) = \binom{12}{10} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \frac{12!}{10!2} \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = \frac{12 \times 11}{2 \times 1} \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = 66 \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = \frac{66}{4096}$$
$$P(X=11) = \binom{12}{11} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \frac{12}{1} \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = 12 \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = \frac{12}{4096}$$
$$P(X=12) = \binom{12}{12} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 1 \left(\frac{1}{4096}\right) = \frac{1}{4096}$$
So,
$$P(X \geq 9) = \frac{220+66+12+1}{4096} = \frac{299}{4096}$$

Final Aner. The final to.
The probability is
$$P(X \geq 9) = \frac{220+66+12+1}{4096} = \frac{299}{4096} \approx 0.073$$

