- \(\Gamma\) is the damping coefficient,
- \(\dot{x}\) is the velocity,
- \(\omega_0\) is the natural frequency of the oscillator,
- \(x\) is the displacement from equilibrium.

This equation describes the motion of a harmonic oscillator that is not driven by any external force but may experience damping. The solution to this equation depends on the relative values of \(\Gamma\) and \(\omega_0\), leading to different damping regimes (strong, critical, or weak).
